    "result_text": "The full suite (AcceptanceTest, the only test class) passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome notification for successful owner creation.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`NotifyWelcome.java`** \u2014 a new OfficeFloor function step that reads the created `Owner` (via `@Val`, so it has the generated id and the assigned memberId) and emits on the dedicated `NOTIFY` logger a line containing both:\n   ```\n   Welcome owner id={} memberId={}\n   ```\n\n2. **Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `notify` step in the create pipeline after `audit` and before `respond`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors. Because it sits on the main create path (not the `respondExisting` idempotent-replay branch), it only fires on an actual successful create \u2014 after `save` and `assignMemberId` have run, so both the id and memberId are populated.\n\nThis mirrors the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern (dedicated named logger via SLF4J), consistent with the repo conventions. The acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and memberId \u2014 passes, as does the rest of the suite. Observed output confirms it:\n\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```",
